## Q5. Development split: share of plain tokens whose word is in the model's top-N words

Tokens scored by the CRF (3 bypassed addresses excluded): 60,593. Plain tokens (`bias` emitted, i.e. not inside an address-dictionary or component phrase): 27,130 (44.8%).
Plain tokens where `bias` is the FIRST state feature (the U block is a prefix, Lemma 2 applies): 9,739 (35.9% of plain). The rest have postcode features (or `commonly X` with zero component types) before `bias`: 17,391.
Of those, without a `prefix`/`suffix` feature (so the key does not need the pre-normalization token): 7,115.
Plain tokens with word count > 50 (not n-gram words): 25,836; count 1..50: 702; unknown (count 0): 592.

